# index.html's CSP pins a sha256 of each of its inline scripts, so the bytes the
# browser receives have to be identical everywhere. Without this line, Windows
# checks the file out as CRLF while GitHub Pages serves the LF that git stores,
# and a hash can only ever match one of the two — and a mismatch is not a
# warning, it is a blank page. Pin the working tree to LF so there is one answer.
#
# scripts/csp-hashes.mjs recomputes the hashes; tests/e2e/csp.spec.js fails if
# they have drifted, which is what stops a stale hash reaching production.
index.html text eol=lf
